# CARSHENAS_TLS_MODE=cdn: a CDN in front (ArvanCloud for carshenas.app, docs/runbooks/deploy.md, "Behind ArvanCloud's CDN").
# The CDN answers visitors over HTTPS with its own certificate and forwards to this server over http (port 80) or https
# (port 443, its default when the origin protocol is left as it is). On 443 this proxy shows a certificate from Caddy's own
# authority, which the CDN accepts for the hop to the origin; visitors never see it. Either way it tells the web app the
# visitor used https (secure cookies, HSTS) and passes on the address the CDN reports, believed only from
# CARSHENAS_TRUSTED_PROXIES. Ports 80 and 443 should be open to the CDN's ranges alone (deploy/host/carshenas-edge-firewall).
http:// {
	import carshenas https
}

https://{$CARSHENAS_SITE_ADDRESS} {
	tls internal
	import carshenas https
}
